WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.700
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and Orphan Black
is back!

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.140
I didn’t catch season 1 till after it finished
airing, but I’ll be doing weekly videos

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.140
for Season 2.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.110
This will be my first one, but in case any
of you aren’t up to speed on what’s going

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:16.260
on I’ll do a super quick recap before my
Top 5 moments.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.730
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do a ton of BBC show videos like Doctor

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.410
Who, Sherlock and Orphan Black.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.020
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.390
So super quick recap of CloneClub season 1.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:34.440
We introduced to the Dyad Clone conflict via
Sarah, and even though the perspective shifts

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.940
based on which Clone is in a scene I always
thought of her as being the main protagonist.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.600
Rachel and Doctor Leekie are essentially the
main villains until we find out about Helena

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.950
who becomes kind of the second big villain
but that only really comes out near the end

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.170
of the season.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:54.670
The Dyad is essentially trying to advance
human genetics and make it so that they can

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:59.829
own human DNA, clone DNA really, but eventually
it’s implied that big Pharmaceutical companies

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.610
will start owning people like you would own
possessions.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.400
Really bad for everyone.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.079
Because all the clones were like a beta trial
for all their human experimentation and they’re

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:11.189
starting to break down a la Katja, the Dyad
corrals them as part of their ongoing research

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:14.590
and Helena, with the aide of the original
cloning scientists starts to hunt down and

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
eliminate them.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.240
So think of the Dyad villains as an allegory
for big pharma treating pushing the idea of

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.540
self-directed evolution through science.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.630
And Helena as like the religous zealot who’s
completely opposed to the idea of self directed

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:27.630
evolution.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:35.009
The clones are the collateral damage and band
together to survive.

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:37.950
So now that we’re caught up I’m going
to do my Top 5 moments from the episode and

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.659
then my review.

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:41.419
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:44.389
Here we go, Number 5 - Alison goes Shopping.

00:01:44.389 --> 00:01:48.859
I love Alison so much, I have a feeling she’s
going to be my favorite Clone this season.

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:52.729
The shopping scene was hilarious and in case
you missed it, every time there was an Alison

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:55.709
scene after this they used the same funny
music cues.

00:01:55.709 --> 00:01:58.929
Like the music would go from really serious
to light and funny.

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:05.409
Meaning, that all of the comedy in the episode
and maybe the season would be flowing from

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:06.409
Alison.

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:08.679
You get this real sense that Alison is a reluctant
participant.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.989
She’s the only one with a traditional home
situation.

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:16.650
So even when she skyped in for a Clone meeting
later you could see her ironing her family's

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.940
laundry in the background.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.909
And then we have to talk about her play.

00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:26.110
Number 4 - Alison’s Play
The play itself is a really funny meta story

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.200
about Alison’s role in the fight against
Dyad as well as a callback to season 1 a la

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.030
cleaning up unfortunate bodies..

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:39.950
I love how they called back to Felix’s Cats
comment about the name of the play.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.319
Who else listened to the actual lyrics they
were singing.

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:45.290
It was all about plasma leaking on the floor
and cleaning up blood.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.970
Which kind of harks back to Cosima and Delphine
with the blood samples.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:54.159
As much as I think this is all Sarah’s story
and the other clones are just in it.

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:55.530
That’s really not true.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:03:01.380
Orphan Black is the overstory all the clones’
stories, so everytime we jump to a scene with

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.599
a different clone, there’s always references
to what’s happening with the other clones.

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:23.969
Like Alison’s play references Cosima’s
blood and Sarah cleaning up Katja’s body.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:33.680
It gets a bit confusing trying to use every
scene to call back to moments from all the

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:41.310
clones, so high fives to the writers for keeping
the narrative so complex and interesting.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:46.499
Number 3 - Sara Tricks Daniel with Alison

00:03:46.499 --> 00:03:51.610
This was one of the funniest attempted abductions
ever.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.900
It was hard to tell if Alison actually knew
it was going to happen because it seemed like

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.250
she was surprised.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.079
She was skyping in while Sarah was planning
how to get into the Dyad, but I think they

00:04:00.079 --> 00:04:03.700
just cut Alison out of the conversation when
they were setting her up as a distraction

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.389
to get Daniel away.

00:04:05.389 --> 00:04:10.170
Side note, I also feel like this was a good
anti-kidnapping PSA, even though they did

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.390
get her in the van eventually.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:17.519
So in case anyone ever tries to abduct you,
blow your rape whistle AND pepper spray the

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:20.310
shit of of anything in your field of vision.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.830
Even though Daniel let her go, they totally
deserved to get maced.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.169
Alison said that she wasn’t keeping guns
at home anymore, but I was surprised she didn’t

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:29.169
have one on her.

00:04:29.169 --> 00:04:35.930
I love how she just accepted Daniel’s apology
and slid out of the Van, like thanks a lot

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.060
asshole bye!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.780
Number 2 - Doctor Leekies Speech

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:43.840
There was a lot going on at the Dyad party,
but it was Leekie’s speech that really interested

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.840
me.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.140
He basically speechify’s the history of
the Dyad and how far their organization reaches

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.140
around the world.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.199
Started in 1918 and now it’s got labs in
over a 100 countries with over 27,000 employees.

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:04.560
It’s the personification of big pharma.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:12.729
Remember his mission, which is tied up in
the philosophy of Neolutionism, is self-directed

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:13.729
evolution.

00:05:13.729 --> 00:05:18.490
That’s why the clones exist and why they
called Kira a biological goldmine.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.150
Leekie believes she’s the next stage of
evolution.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.259
The clones on the other hand are breaking
down slowly.

00:05:25.259 --> 00:05:32.910
In case you missed it, they made their plan
of owning human DNA a lot clearer during Rachel’s

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:33.910
meeting with the Koreans.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.949
and my Number 1 moment - Helena is still alive.

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:40.169
This was like the major WTF of the episode.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:44.229
Sarah and Art put the pieces together after
he explains what was going on with the Diner

00:05:44.229 --> 00:05:45.229
attack.

00:05:45.229 --> 00:05:47.690
I liked that they called them religous zealots.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:51.099
They looked creepy when I just thought they
were working for Rachel.

00:05:51.099 --> 00:05:54.479
Who buttons that top button without wearing
anything around their neck.

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:56.949
Matt Smith’s Doctor would be rolling in
his grave.

00:05:56.949 --> 00:06:01.030
Helena’s plan seems pretty simple, just
kill all the clones.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:04.520
Right now I don’t think she has any grand
design.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.319
She literally just wants them all dead.

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:11.090
I don’t think she intends to hurt Kira,
but she might kill Mrs S.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:13.520
I actually checked the Orphan Black hashtag
on Twitter right as the episode was ending

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:19.470
and it was just an endless stream of HELENAs
in all caps.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:25.629
Let me know what your favorite moment was,
Alison’s Play, the Helena reveal or something

00:06:25.629 --> 00:06:26.629
else?

00:06:26.629 --> 00:06:31.270
And let me know who your favorite clone was
this week.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:37.660
Here’s a couple more really important moments
that weren’t my favorite, but that we need

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.529
to talk about in the comments.

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:42.560
Cosima and Delphine, who is playing who the
best?

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.060
Cosima is definitely on team Clone Club, but
there’s this spy versus spy thing going

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.380
on with Delphine working with Leekie to get
Cosima on their side.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:54.659
I think underneath it all Delphine isn’t
as geniuine as say Art, who’s trying to

00:06:54.659 --> 00:06:57.250
get Sarah to trust him.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.370
Delphine didn’t realize she was kissing
Sarah till after their whole run in with Leekie.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.240
You’d think that if you were in love with
someone and had been in a relationship, you’d

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.940
know if the person you were kissing was someone
else.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.169
Plus Sarah’s hair wasn’t even the same.

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:13.259
Maybe Delphine is just the worst girlfriend
ever?

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:15.370
As for Art I think he’ll be a force for
good.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.730
Even if he’s technically not on Team Clone
Club.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.190
The same goes for Paul.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:23.060
He’s playing both sides, but I think he
really cares about Sarah.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:27.729
I don’t think any of those double agent
relationships will end well, Delphine or Paul.

00:07:27.729 --> 00:07:32.039
Overall though I gave the episode an A minus,
it was a great entry to season 2.

00:07:32.039 --> 00:07:36.840
Especially considering that the hardest job
the show has is topping itself.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:43.539
Season 1 was so good it’s going to be hard
to keep one-upping the stakes.

00:07:43.539 --> 00:07:44.539
Enter Helena.

00:07:44.539 --> 00:07:51.560
I think part of the solution and the episode
explained it beautifully, is to go international.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:55.889
Season 1 was fairly self contained geographically.

00:07:55.889 --> 00:07:59.780
Remember how Rachel was asking Paul all those
questions about speaking Mandarin and going

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.780
to Taiwan.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:05.310
That also ties back into Leekie’s speech
about Dyad having offices all over the world.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:09.490
The story of season 2 is just going to be
told from a much more global context.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:13.379
The only thing I thought could have be done
better was Felix’s story in the episode.

00:08:13.379 --> 00:08:17.770
He, just like Alison was just a well of comedy
they used to drive the plot forward.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:20.590
But Alison’s scenes were all so complex
and interesting, they kind of made Felix seem

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.970
like the throwaway character this week.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.430
The fool essentially.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:28.439
Although I kind of think of his archetype
as the fool.

00:08:28.439 --> 00:08:33.830
Not in a bad way though.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.960
I kind of go into hyper aware mode whenever
the clones are all together in a scene.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:41.520
I kind of think of them as different aspects
of the freudian psyche.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.390
Like one clone is the id, one is the ego and
one is the superego.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:49.660
I guess you could also divide them into the
subconscious and conscious.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:50.950
But let me know if you agree.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:53.850
Like when they’re all together, they’re
like a whole person, they’re all pieces

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:58.960
of a single person.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.850
Like I said, I’m going to be doing weekly
videos for episodes every Saturday night.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.660
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:08.240
Tomorrow is Game of Thrones episode 3, so
to start getting ready for that, here’s

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:12.760
my video for last week’s episode and here’s
my latest Doctor Who series 8 video.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:13.950
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:14.290
High Fives!

